# statement committed inside the transaction: statement mark moves from 0 to 1
# COMMIT of a multi-statement transaction (statement: COMMIT): boundary reached, accumulator holds 0 rows, in_sub_stmt=0, open tables in THD: none
# COMMIT of a multi-statement transaction (statement: COMMIT): test.t1 enters the firing chain at depth 1; it is closed, transactional MDL_SHARED_WRITE held: yes; re-opening it to reach its triggers
# COMMIT of a multi-statement transaction (statement: COMMIT): FIRE test.t1_commit (AFTER INSERT,UPDATE,DELETE BEFORE COMMIT, order 1) over positions [0, 1): 0 INSERT, 0 UPDATE, 0 DELETE rows; body would run here: execute_trigger() as root@localhost, SUB_STMT_TRIGGER
